"GCRA admission for a limit of 5 per second: a burst of five, then one "
"every 200 ms."
msgstr "毎秒5件の上限でのGCRAによる許可：5件のバーストの後、200 msごとに1件。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:505
msgid "Worked example: five per second by hand"
msgstr "例題：毎秒5件を手で計算する"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:507
msgid ""
"Take :math:`N = 5` and :math:`W = 1000` ms, so :math:`T = 200` ms and "
":math:`\\tau = 800` ms, and let a client that has been idle send six "
"requests at :math:`t = 0`. The first finds an empty cell: "
":math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = \\max(0, 0) = 0 \\le 800`, so it conforms and "
":math:`\\mathrm{TAT} \\leftarrow 200`. The next four conform the same way "
"and leave :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = 1000`. The sixth finds :math:`1000 > 0 + "
"800` and is refused with ``Retry-After`` :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} - \\tau - t "
"= 200` ms. At :math:`t = 199` a request still finds :math:`1000 > 999` "
"and is refused; at :math:`t = 200` it finds :math:`1000 \\le 1000`, "
"conforms, and leaves :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = 1200`. The unit test "
"``gcra_admits_exactly_the_burst_then_drains_at_the_emission_rate`` in "
"``crates/store/src/limiter.rs`` checks exactly these numbers."
msgstr ""
":math:`N = 5`\\ 、\\ :math:`W = 1000`\\ msとすると、\\ :math:`T = 200`\\ ms、\\ "
":math:`\\tau = 800`\\ msです。アイドル状態だったクライアントが\\ :math:`t = 0`\\ "
"で6件のリクエストを送るとします。1件目は空のセルを見つけます。\\ :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = \\max(0, 0) = 0 "
"\\le 800`\\ なので適合し、\\ :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} \\leftarrow 200`\\ "
"となります。続く4件も同じように適合し、\\ :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = 1000`\\ を残します。6件目は\\ "
":math:`1000 > 0 + 800`\\ となり、\\ ``Retry-After`` :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} - "
"\\tau - t = 200`\\ msで拒否されます。\\ :math:`t = 199`\\ でのリクエストもまだ\\ "
":math:`1000 > 999`\\ となって拒否されます。\\ :math:`t = 200`\\ では\\ :math:`1000 "
"\\le 1000`\\ となって適合し、\\ :math:`\\mathrm{TAT} = 1200`\\ を残します。\\ "
"``crates/store/src/limiter.rs``\\ の単体テスト\\ "
"``gcra_admits_exactly_the_burst_then_drains_at_the_emission_rate``\\ "
"は、まさにこれらの数値を確かめます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:509
msgid "Implementation: ``arrive``"
msgstr "実装：\\ ``arrive``"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:511
msgid ""
"Applies one arrival to the cells of a locked shard and returns the "
"decision, the retry delay and the remaining budget. In "
"``crates/store/src/limiter.rs`` (crate ``sibuna-store``)."
msgstr ""
"ロックしたシャードのセルに到着を一つ適用し、判定、再試行までの遅延、残りの予算を返します。\\ "
"``crates/store/src/limiter.rs``\\ （クレート\\ ``sibuna-store``\\ ）にあります。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:513
msgid ""
"fn arrive(\n"
"    cells: &mut [Cell; SLOTS_PER_SHARD],\n"
"    key: u64,\n"
"    now_ms: u64,\n"
"    limits: Limits,\n"
") -> Decision {\n"
"    let interval = limits.emission_interval();\n"
"    let tau = limits.burst_tolerance();\n"
"    let Some(cell) = locate(cells, key, now_ms, tau) else {\n"
"        return Decision {\n"
"            limited: true,\n"
"            capacity_exhausted: true,\n"
"            retry_after_ms: interval,\n"
"            remaining: 0,\n"
"        };\n"
"    };\n"
"    let tat = cell.tat_ms.max(now_ms);\n"
"    let horizon = now_ms.saturating_add(tau);\n"
"    if tat > horizon {\n"
"        return Decision {\n"
"            limited: true,\n"
"            capacity_exhausted: false,\n"
"            retry_after_ms: tat - tau - now_ms,\n"
"            remaining: 0,\n"
"        };\n"
"    }\n"
"    cell.tat_ms = tat.saturating_add(interval);\n"
"    // ... remaining = min(rate, floor((t + tau - TAT) / T) + 1)\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"fn arrive(\n"
"    cells: &mut [Cell; SLOTS_PER_SHARD],\n"
"    key: u64,\n"
"    now_ms: u64,\n"
"    limits: Limits,\n"
") -> Decision {\n"
"    let interval = limits.emission_interval();\n"
"    let tau = limits.burst_tolerance();\n"
"    let Some(cell) = locate(cells, key, now_ms, tau) else {\n"
"        return Decision {\n"
"            limited: true,\n"
"            capacity_exhausted: true,\n"
"            retry_after_ms: interval,\n"
"            remaining: 0,\n"
"        };\n"
"    };\n"
"    let tat = cell.tat_ms.max(now_ms);\n"
"    let horizon = now_ms.saturating_add(tau);\n"
"    if tat > horizon {\n"
"        return Decision {\n"
"            limited: true,\n"
"            capacity_exhausted: false,\n"
"            retry_after_ms: tat - tau - now_ms,\n"
"            remaining: 0,\n"
"        };\n"
"    }\n"
"    cell.tat_ms = tat.saturating_add(interval);\n"
"    // ... remaining = min(rate, floor((t + tau - TAT) / T) + 1)\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:545
msgid ""
"The shard's ``check`` takes the lock and calls ``arrive`` with the locked "
"cells; the guard releases the lock when ``check`` returns. Cells are 16 "
"bytes (a key and a TAT) in 16 shards of 512 slots with a 16-slot probe "
"window, about 128 KiB in all. A cell whose TAT is older than :math:`t - "
"\\tau` has drained and is reclaimed on the spot. The ``Retry-After`` header "
"is computed from the same arithmetic. Saturated probe windows refuse new "
"clients rather than evicting active quota state, and the decision says so "
"(``capacity_exhausted``), so a caller does not escalate a saturation "
"refusal into a ban. A zero configured rate refuses requests. One limiter "
"serves several rules: the cell key is a Wyhash of the client address seeded "
"with the rule's scope, so the same client in different scopes has "
"independent budgets."
msgstr ""
"シャードの\\ ``check``\\ はロックを取り、ロックしたセルを渡して\\ ``arrive``\\ を呼び出します。ガードは\\ ``check``\\ "
"が戻るときにロックを解放します。セルは16バイト（キーとTAT）で、16スロットの探査窓を持つ512スロットのシャードが16個、全体で約128 "
"KiBです。TATが\\ :math:`t - \\tau`\\ より古いセルは空になっており、その場で回収されます。\\ ``Retry-After``\\ "
"ヘッダーも同じ算術で計算します。探査窓が飽和すると、有効なクォータの状態を追い出すのではなく新しいクライアントを拒否し、判定もそのことを示します（\\ "
"``capacity_exhausted``\\ ）。そのため呼び出し側は、飽和による拒否を禁止へと格上げしません。設定したレートがゼロなら、"
"リクエストを拒否します。一つのリミッターが複数のルールに使われます。セルのキーはルールのスコープをシードにしたクライアントアドレスのWyhashなので、"
"異なるスコープの同じクライアントは独立した予算を持ちます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:547
msgid "The Versioned Ban Table"
msgstr "バージョン付きの禁止テーブル"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:550
msgid ""
"Bans use 4,096 slots with atomic version, key and expiry fields, "
"open-addressed by a keyed hash of the banned address with an 8-slot probe "
"window. A writer, serialised with the other writers by a mutex, brackets "
"each update with version increments; readers take no lock, accept only a "
"stable even version, and retry concurrent changes."
msgstr ""
"禁止には、アトミックなバージョン、キー、期限のフィールドを持つ4,096個のスロットを使います。禁止したアドレスの鍵付きハッシュでオープンアドレス法により配置し、探査窓は8スロットです。書き手は他の書き手とミューテックスで直列化され、各更新をバージョンの増加で挟みます。読み手はロックを取らず、安定した偶数のバージョンだけを受け入れ、並行する変更があれば再試行します。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:552
msgid "Implementation: ``BanTable::ban`` and ``BanTable::read_slot``"
msgstr "実装：\\ ``BanTable::ban``\\ と\\ ``BanTable::read_slot``"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:554
msgid ""
"The writer's bracket and the reader's consistent snapshot. In "
"``crates/store/src/ban_table.rs`` (crate ``sibuna-store``)."
msgstr ""
"書き手による挟み込みと、読み手による一貫したスナップショットです。\\ ``crates/store/src/ban_table.rs``\\ "
"（クレート\\ ``sibuna-store``\\ ）にあります。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:556
msgid ""
"pub fn ban(&self, banned: &[u8], until: u64, now: u64) {\n"
"    let key = slot_key(banned);\n"
"    let _writers = self.lock_writers();\n"
"    let victim = &self.slots[self.victim(key, now)];\n"
"    // A key and an expiry are one logical value: bracket the replacement "
"with\n"
"    // an odd version so readers cannot combine an old key with the next "
"key's\n"
"    // expiry.\n"
"    victim.version.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.until.store(until, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.key.store(key, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.version.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn read_slot(&self, slot: &Slot) -> (u64, u64) {\n"
"    loop {\n"
"        let before = slot.version.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        if before & 1 != 0 {\n"
"            std::hint::spin_loop();\n"
"            continue;\n"
"        }\n"
"        let key = slot.key.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        let until = slot.until.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        if before == slot.version.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {\n"
"            return (key, until);\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"pub fn ban(&self, banned: &[u8], until: u64, now: u64) {\n"
"    let key = slot_key(banned);\n"
"    let _writers = self.lock_writers();\n"
"    let victim = &self.slots[self.victim(key, now)];\n"
"    // キーと期限は論理的に一つの値。置き換えを奇数のバージョンで挟み、\n"
"    // 読み手が古いキーと次のキーの期限を組み合わせられないようにする。\n"
"    victim.version.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.until.store(until, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.key.store(key, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"    victim.version.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"fn read_slot(&self, slot: &Slot) -> (u64, u64) {\n"
"    loop {\n"
"        let before = slot.version.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        if before & 1 != 0 {\n"
"            std::hint::spin_loop();\n"
"            continue;\n"
"        }\n"
"        let key = slot.key.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        let until = slot.until.load(Ordering::SeqCst);\n"
"        if before == slot.version.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {\n"
"            return (key, until);\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:586
msgid ""
"Sequential consistency prevents mixing an old identity with a replacement "
"expiry: every access belongs to one total order, which keeps the argument "
"simple. Readers take no mutex, but can wait for a writer and are not "
"wait-free. These atomic operations have real cost, measured indirectly in "
"the HTTP harness rather than assumed free. A full probe window overwrites "
"a slot that has expired, or else the slot that expires first. ``clear`` "
"lifts every ban but leaves the keys in place, because an emptied slot "
"could hide a colliding key later in a probe chain."
msgstr ""
"逐次一貫性によって、古い識別子と置き換え後の期限が混ざることを防ぎます。すべてのアクセスが一つの全順序に属するので、議論が単純になります。読み手はミューテックスを取りませんが、書き手を待つことがあり、ウェイトフリーではありません。これらのアトミック操作には実際のコストがあり、無償と仮定するのではなく、HTTPのハーネスで間接的に測定しています。探査窓が満杯なら、期限切れのスロットを、なければ最も早く期限が切れるスロットを上書きします。\\ "
"``clear``\\ "
"はすべての禁止を解除しますが、キーはその場に残します。空にしたスロットが、探査の連鎖の先にある衝突したキーを隠してしまい得るからです。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:588
msgid "The MPSC Incident Ring"
msgstr "MPSCインシデントリング"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:591
msgid ""
"When the Shield surface denies a request or the honeypot fires, the "
"incident is copied into a fixed record of about 1.3 KB (client address, "
"User-Agent, method, path, category and payload, each cut at its capacity) "
"and pushed onto a bounded multi-producer single-consumer ring (Vyukov's "
"sequence-stamped design, 512 slots, ``BoundedQueue<IncidentRecord, "
"512>``). Producers are connection threads; the consumer is the storage "
"thread. A full ring drops the newest record rather than blocking a "
"response, an explicit loss policy rather than a durability guarantee. The "
"drop counter makes that loss observable."
msgstr ""
"Shieldの運用構成がリクエストを拒否したり、ハニーポットが反応したりすると、インシデントは約1.3 "
"KBの固定のレコード（クライアントのアドレス、User-Agent、メソッド、パス、カテゴリー、ペイロードで、それぞれ容量で切り詰めます）にコピーされ、上限のある複数生産者・単一消費者のリング（Vyukovのシーケンス番号付きの設計、512スロット、\\ "
"``BoundedQueue<IncidentRecord, 512>``\\ "
"）に積まれます。生産者は接続スレッドで、消費者はストレージスレッドです。リングが満杯なら、応答をブロックするのではなく最も新しいレコードを捨てます。これは永続性の保証ではなく、明示的な損失のポリシーです。破棄のカウンターによって、その損失を観測できます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:593
msgid ""
"/// Copies `incident` into the ring; a full ring drops it and counts the "
"drop.\n"
"pub(crate) fn record(&self, incident: &Incident<'_>) {\n"
"    if self.queue.push(IncidentRecord::from_incident(incident)).is_err() {\n"
"        self.metrics.incidents_dropped.bump();\n"
"    }\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"/// `incident`をリングにコピーする。リングが満杯なら捨てて、その件数を数える。\n"
"pub(crate) fn record(&self, incident: &Incident<'_>) {\n"
"    if self.queue.push(IncidentRecord::from_incident(incident)).is_err() {\n"
"        self.metrics.incidents_dropped.bump();\n"
"    }\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:602
msgid ""
"After moving a record into a pending batch, the storage thread retains "
"it, together with the prepared rows, until the commit is confirmed; it "
"does not silently discard it on a database error, and a retry writes the "
"identical batch."
msgstr ""
"ストレージスレッドは、レコードを保留中のバッチに移した後、コミットが確認されるまで、用意した行とともにそれを保持します。データベースのエラーで黙って捨てることはなく、再試行では同一のバッチを書き込みます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:604
msgid ""
"Each slot carries a sequence number that tells producers whether the slot "
"is free and the consumer whether it is full, so neither side takes a "
"lock. A ring like this cannot be written in safe Rust: producers and the "
"consumer touch different slots of one array at the same time, and only "
"the sequence protocol, not the type system, proves which thread may touch "
"which slot. The module ``crates/store/src/ring.rs`` therefore holds its "
"values in ``UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<T>>`` slots, and each ``unsafe`` block "
"names the step of the protocol that justifies it:"
msgstr ""
"各スロットはシーケンス番号を持ち、それによって生産者はスロットが空いているかを、消費者はスロットが埋まっているかを知ります。そのため、どちらの側もロックを取りません。このようなリングは安全なRustでは書けません。生産者と消費者が一つの配列の異なるスロットに同時に触れ、どのスレッドがどのスロットに触れてよいかを証明するのは型システムではなくシーケンスのプロトコルだけだからです。そのためモジュール\\ "
"``crates/store/src/ring.rs``\\ は値を\\ ``UnsafeCell<MaybeUninit<T>>``\\ "
"のスロットに保持し、各\\ ``unsafe``\\ ブロックは、それを正当化するプロトコルの手順を名指しします。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:606
msgid ""
"if diff == 0 {\n"
"    // Relaxed: the CAS only arbitrates which producer owns position `pos`.\n"
"    match self.tail.0.compare_exchange_weak(\n"
"        pos, pos.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Relaxed, Ordering::Relaxed,\n"
"    ) {\n"
"        Ok(_) => {\n"
"            // SAFETY: the CAS gave this thread position `pos`, and\n"
"            // `sequence == pos` says the slot is empty; no other producer "
"can\n"
"            // claim `pos` and the consumer does not read it before the "
"Release\n"
"            // store below.\n"
"            unsafe { (*slot.value.get()).write(value) };\n"
"            // Release: publishes the written value to the consumer.\n"
"            slot.sequence.store(pos.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Release);\n"
"            return Ok(());\n"
"        }\n"
"        Err(current) => pos = current,\n"
"    }\n"
"} else if diff < 0 {\n"
"    return Err(value);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"if diff == 0 {\n"
"    // Relaxed：CASは、どの生産者が位置`pos`を持つかを決めるだけ。\n"
"    match self.tail.0.compare_exchange_weak(\n"
"        pos, pos.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Relaxed, Ordering::Relaxed,\n"
"    ) {\n"
"        Ok(_) => {\n"
"            // SAFETY: CASによってこのスレッドが位置`pos`を得ており、\n"
"            // `sequence == pos`はスロットが空であることを示す。他の生産者は\n"
"            // `pos`を取得できず、消費者は下のReleaseストアより前には\n"
"            // これを読まない。\n"
"            unsafe { (*slot.value.get()).write(value) };\n"
"            // Release：書き込んだ値を消費者に公開する。\n"
"            slot.sequence.store(pos.wrapping_add(1), Ordering::Release);\n"
"            return Ok(());\n"
"        }\n"
"        Err(current) => pos = current,\n"
"    }\n"
"} else if diff < 0 {\n"
"    return Err(value);\n"
"}"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:629
msgid ""
"Two conventions of the ring are types, not comments. On a full ring "
"``push`` returns ``Err(value)``, handing the record back so the caller "
"decides whether to count or drop it; a bare ``false`` would lose it. The "
"ring has a single consumer, and ``pop`` takes ``&mut self``, and shared "
"code must claim the unique ``Consumer`` first, so a second consumer does "
"not compile or is refused at run time."
msgstr ""
"リングの二つの約束事は、コメントではなく型になっています。リングが満杯のとき、\\ ``push``\\ は\\ ``Err(value)``\\ "
"を返してレコードを返却し、数えるか捨てるかを呼び出し側に決めさせます。単なる\\ ``false``\\ "
"ではレコードが失われます。リングの消費者は一つで、\\ ``pop``\\ は\\ ``&mut self``\\ "
"を取り、共有されたコードはまず唯一の\\ ``Consumer``\\ "
"を取得しなければなりません。そのため二つ目の消費者はコンパイルできないか、実行時に拒否されます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:631
msgid "Read-Copy-Update Engine Publication"
msgstr "read-copy-updateによるエンジンの公開"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:634
msgid ""
"The policy engine is rebuilt off the hot path when policies change. "
"Requests must never observe a half-built engine, and an engine must never "
"be freed while a request is still reading it. Sibuna publishes each engine "
"as an ``Arc<Engine>`` in an ``EngineSlot``, and each connection reads it "
"through an ``EngineCache``:"
msgstr ""
"ポリシーが変わると、ポリシーエンジンはホットパスの外で再構築されます。リクエストが作りかけのエンジンを目にしてはならず、"
"リクエストがまだ読んでいる間にエンジンが解放されてもなりません。Sibunaは各エンジンを\\ ``EngineSlot``\\ の中の\\ "
"``Arc<Engine>``\\ として公開し、各接続は\\ ``EngineCache``\\ を通してそれを読みます。"

#: ../../zero-allocation.rst:637
msgid ""
"The storage thread builds Engine v2 off the request path and publishes it "
"into the EngineSlot, which holds an RwLock around the current Arc and an "
"atomic generation. Connection thread A has refreshed: its cache holds "
"generation 2 and an Arc of Engine v2, and its next refresh is one acquire "
"load with no clone. Connection thread B still holds generation 1 and an Arc "
"of Engine v1; on its next refresh it sees the generation moved, takes the "
"read lock and clones the Arc of v2. Engine v1 is freed when B lets go of it."
msgstr ""
"ストレージスレッドはリクエスト経路の外でEngine v2を構築し、EngineSlotに公開します。EngineSlotは、"
"現在のArcを囲むRwLockとアトミックな世代を持ちます。接続スレッドAは更新済みで、そのキャッシュは世代2とEngine v2のArcを持ち、"
"次の更新はクローンなしのacquireロード一回です。接続スレッドBはまだ世代1とEngine v1のArcを持っており、"
"次の更新で世代が進んだことに気づくと、読み込みロックを取ってv2のArcをクローンします。Engine v1は、Bがそれを手放したときに解放されます。"

